# shell: desktop
# home: fixture
# prefs: factory
# Find drops a bar under the toolbar; Return walks the hits and wraps,
# and the hit becomes the SELECTION, so a character typed over it
# replaces it.  For a BASIC file a NUMBER is a line to GO to -- not the
# first place those digits appear as text, but the line that WEARS the
# number -- proven by putting the same digits both places and reading
# back which one a typed character replaced.
wait 25
click 980 30
wait 4
menu-pick Programming
wait 4
menu-pick TikuBasic
wait 150
click 71 8
wait 8
menu-pick Open Project…
wait 40
click 400 220
wait 6
click 675 413
wait 60
click-window Project
wait 8
key Down
wait 8
key Return
wait 90
expect-title main.bas
note the find bar drops in, its label saying a number here is a line
key f ctrl
wait 8
expect-pixel 198 293 000000
note a number goes to the LINE that WEARS it -- line 40, not the "40"
note that sits as text on the first line -- and its number is selected
key 4
key 0
wait 4
key Return
wait 8
key Escape
wait 4
key X shift
wait 6
click 205 268
wait 60
expect-file-has /tmp/trk_home/main.bas X done
expect-file-has /tmp/trk_home/main.bas say 40 here
note a word is walked by Return, and the THIRD hit wraps to the first
key f ctrl
wait 8
key h
key e
key r
key e
wait 4
key Return
wait 6
key Return
wait 6
key Return
wait 6
key Escape
wait 4
key z
wait 6
click 205 268
wait 60
expect-file-has /tmp/trk_home/main.bas 10 say 40 z
expect-file-has /tmp/trk_home/main.bas 30 say here
quit
